   // Frame-scoped.
   std::vector<gfx::Rect> inline3d_frosted_rects_;
 
+  // DisplayXR inline-3D (browser#120): MONO UNDER FROST — for each tile whose
+  // canvas quad is SUPPRESSED and over which a frosted rect sits, the frosted
+  // rects that sit over it, keyed by that tile's own canvas quad.
+  //
+  // WHY IT EXISTS. Inside a frosted rect the region is drawn by NOBODY: the
+  // canvas quad was withheld from the page raster (display.cc suppression) and
+  // the woven draw-back is clipped out of the rect by D' above. The page's
+  // backdrop-filter pass then blurs a dark void and the frosted card reads
+  // black. D' says "depth behind the glass reads FLAT" — this list is what
+  // makes flat literally true instead of empty.
+  //
+  // WHY IT IS KEYED BY THE CANVAS QUAD, and why that is the whole fix.
+  // ORDERING IS THE BUG. Skia samples a backdrop filter from whatever is
+  // already on the canvas at saveLayer time (skia_renderer.cc,
+  // DrawRenderPassQuad), so the mono content has to be in the page raster
+  // BEFORE the frosted pass draws — not repaired afterwards, when the glass is
+  // already composited over a void. The tile's canvas quad is the one draw
+  // that is guaranteed to precede it: ComputeInline3dPlaneSplit only records a
+  // frosted rect for a quad at front-to-back index i < k(T), i.e. strictly IN
+  // FRONT of the tile, and DrawRenderPassOnGpu walks the quad list
+  // BackToFront — so index k is painted before index i, always.
+  //
+  // Frame-scoped, cleared with the other three lists. The pointers are into
+  // the current frame's quad list, exactly like |inline3d_over_clips_|; empty
+  // (and never consulted) when the flag is off or nothing is frosted.
+  base::flat_map<const DrawQuad*, absl::InlinedVector<gfx::Rect, 2>>
+      inline3d_mono_clips_;
+
   bool visible_ = false;
   bool disable_color_checks_for_testing_ = false;
 
